[s0l0!-header][h1]Headers[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

C++ offers various headers, each of which contains information needed for programs to work properly. 
We have already seen the standard [b]<iostream>[/b] header on our first C++ program:
[code format="cpp" ][b]#include <iostream>[/b]
using namespace std;

int main()
{
cout << "Hello world!";
return 0;
} [/code]
[b]#include[/b] is used for adding a standard or user-defined header files to the program.
[note]The [b]<iostream>[/b] header defines the standard stream objects that input and output data.[/note]

