[s0l0!-header][h1]Namespaces[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

A [b]namespace[/b] is a declarative region that provides a scope to the identifiers (names of elements) inside it.
In our code, the line [b]using namespace std;[/b] tells the compiler to use the std (standard) namespace:
[code format="cpp" ]#include <iostream>
[b]using namespace std;[/b]

int main()
{
cout << "Hello world!";
return 0;
} [/code]
[note]The [b]std[/b] namespace includes features of the [b]C++ Standard Library[/b].[/note]

